+future authenticated-cache transaction and is not claimed by Artifact v1.
+
+### ArtifactCache v1
+
+`ArtifactCache` is the only physical compiler-artifact cache. Its v1 API is
+limited to `lookup(request, build_spec)` and atomic
+`publish(artifact, request, build_spec)`. It has no compile callback, eviction,
+deletion, CUDA loader or framework surface. The key is exclusively
+`Artifact.get_cache_key_digest_for(request, build_spec)`; device identity,
+loader compatibility, cache root and model/framework data do not enter it.
+
+The caller supplies an existing absolute canonical non-root directory owned by
+the effective user with exact mode `0700`. Linux opens the whole root path with
+`openat2` no-symlink resolution, rejects writable non-sticky ancestors, and
+creates only this fixed owner-private layout:
+
+```text
+<root>/pypto-nvidia-artifacts/v1/sha256/<first-two-hex>/<64-hex>.artifact
+```
+
+Every component and entry is opened descriptor-relatively without following
+symlinks. A final entry must be one owner-owned regular file, mode `0400`, link
+count one and size 1 through 68 MiB. The reader bounds before allocation, uses
+exact positioned reads, rechecks metadata, performs full canonical Artifact
+deserialization against the expected request/build spec, and compares the full
+cache-key projection with the digest-derived filename. Only `ENOENT` is a
+cache miss; corruption, permission, type, provenance or canonical failures are
+errors and ordinary lookup never mutates the cache.
+
+Publication first round-trips the candidate against the exact request/spec. It
+writes a random same-shard exclusive temporary file, syncs and reads back the
+complete bytes, changes it to mode `0400`, syncs again, then publishes with
+`renameat2(RENAME_NOREPLACE)` and syncs the shard directory. A concurrent
+winner is accepted only when its fully revalidated canonical bytes are exactly
+identical; a different or corrupt winner is a fatal conflict and is never
+replaced. A failed writer removes only its own temporary name. Broad
+scavenging, quarantine and self-healing are not v1 behavior.
+
+The cache handle is bound to its creator process and rejected after `fork`;
+each child constructs its own handle while all coordination remains in atomic
+filesystem primitives. V1 has no cache-wide quota or eviction: `ENOSPC` fails
+publication, so capacity management is an explicit availability task rather
+than a correctness claim. The cache contains no CUDA handle, device query,
+module, stream, workspace, online tuning or framework state. It remains a
+trusted-local cache, not authenticated storage.
